# Testing conventions

Tests make NO real network calls: mock the Open-Meteo HTTP layer (httpx
`MockTransport`) and set `POLLER_ENABLED=false` so the live poller never starts
during tests. Each test uses an isolated temporary SQLite database. Detection
logic is tested with hand-constructed synthetic reading sequences that assert
exactly which events fire and which do NOT — the application code must stay
testable this way: detectors are pure functions (readings in, events out) with
no I/O, and thresholds/windows are named constants. Detection tests are the most
important tests in the suite.

**Rationale:** deterministic, network-free tests are required for reliable CI,
and controlled synthetic sequences are the only way to prove the detection logic
fires precisely as designed.
